    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 48 tests pass, including the new Cp35 test. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a different telephone, it's still created and flagged with `possibleDuplicate: true` / `possibleDuplicateOf: <matching owner id>`; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema (`possibleDuplicate` boolean, `possibleDuplicateOf` int32), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` columns with getters/setters (the GET re-reads from the DB, so the values must be persisted).\n- **Schema DDL** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `findPossibleDuplicateOf(...)`, which (after the hard-duplicate check has passed) scans existing owners for one that shares the new owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` with a different normalized telephone, choosing the lowest matching id. `addOwner` sets `possibleDuplicate` from whether a match was found and stores `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\nMapStruct maps the two new fields automatically by name, so no mapper change was needed. The full suite (48 tests) is green.",
